              "type": "Type"
            }
          ],
          "content": "God never intended to deprive Abraham of his only son, but simply to test his faith. Rembrandt depicted the horrifying scene in a highly intimate manner. The unshackled Isaac does not put up a struggle. Abraham covers his son’s eyes to spare him the sight of the knife he wields. An angel steps in just in the nick of time."
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "classified_as": [
            {
